# A Computer-Aided Exercise for Checking Novices' Understanding of Market Equilibrium Changes.

**Authors:** Katz, Arnold

## Abstract
Describes a computer-aided supplement to the introductory microeconomics course that enhances students' understanding with simulation-based tools for reviewing what they have learned from lectures and conventional textbooks about comparing market equilibria. Includes a discussion of students' learning progressions and retention after using the program. (DSK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ588681

